# The network of "Fast from far away": the office, the internet, the site's
# firewall, the shop's server in its far region, the long private link and
# the DR site.
#
#   office 192.0.2.10 --- isp --- fw --- shop eth0 203.0.113.10
#                                        shop eth1 10.0.5.10 --- wan --- dr1 10.0.6.20
#
# isp stands for the internet between the office and the site: 50 ms each
# way, a 100 ms round trip. fw is the site's firewall, a router in front of
# shop. wan is the private link to the DR site: 50 Mbit/s towards dr1, with
# 50 ms each way (a 100 ms round trip), and 1% of the packets towards dr1
# lost at random. isp and wan are scenery.
machine office
machine isp router
machine fw router
machine shop
machine wan router
machine dr1

link office:eth0=192.0.2.10/24 isp:office=192.0.2.1/24
link isp:fw=198.51.100.1/30 fw:isp=198.51.100.2/30
link fw:shop=203.0.113.1/24 shop:eth0=203.0.113.10/24
link shop:eth1=10.0.5.10/24 wan:shop=10.0.5.1/24
link wan:dr1=10.0.6.1/24 dr1:eth0=10.0.6.20/24

route office default via 192.0.2.1
route isp 203.0.113.0/24 via 198.51.100.2
route fw default via 198.51.100.1
route shop default via 203.0.113.1
route shop 10.0.6.0/24 via 10.0.5.1
route dr1 default via 10.0.6.1

# The internet's delay, both ways.
netem isp office delay 50ms limit 2000
netem isp fw delay 50ms limit 2000
# The private link: towards dr1, where the archive goes, its speed, its
# delay and its loss; back towards shop, where the acknowledgements go, the
# delay only.
netem wan dr1 rate 50mbit delay 50ms loss 1% limit 2000
netem wan shop delay 50ms limit 2000

run fw nftables
